---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="VIOT — Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">Project Overview</p>
    <h1>Virtual Ion-Optics <span class="accent">Testbed</span></h1>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      <p>A multiscale assessment of carbon-nanomaterial accelerator-grid coatings for charge-exchange (CEX) erosion mitigation in the NASA NSTAR ion thruster.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <div class="grid-2">
      <h2 class="kicker text-muted">The Problem</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Gridded ion thrusters accelerate Xe⁺ electrostatically. Fast beam ions undergo resonant charge exchange with slow neutrals, creating slow CEX ions born inside the accelerating field. These are pulled into the negatively biased accelerator grid, sputtering it.</p>
        <p><strong>This is the dominant end-of-life mechanism for ion thrusters.</strong></p>
        <p>Our research asks: Can thin nanostructured carbon coatings on a conventional Mo grid capture the sputter resistance of bulk carbon grids, without the structural/thermal/manufacturing penalties of monolithic carbon optics?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <p class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">Core Hypotheses</p>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-grid">
        <span class="card-id">H1</span>
        <p class="card-stmt">GNP and/or graphene coatings reduce accelerator-grid erosion</p>
        <div class="card-divider">
          <span class="card-verdict card-verdict--confirmed">Partially confirmed</span>
          <p class="card-evidence">GNP reduces erosion 1.39–4.23×. Graphene worsens it (0.37–0.85×, i.e. up to 2.7× more mass loss). Cross-run CV &lt; 0.57% on all 12 cases — the material separation is orders of magnitude above numerical noise.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <div class="card-grid">
        <span class="card-id">H2</span>
        <p class="card-stmt">Graphene "transparency" diminishes; penetrative energy transfer dominates</p>
        <div class="card-divider">
          <span class="card-verdict card-verdict--warning">Confirmed, sign reversed</span>
          <p class="card-evidence">A heavy Xe ion at CEX energies passes through the monolayer, depositing momentum in the Mo substrate; the low-thermal-coupling sheet cannot dissipate the cascade, so it ejects several carbon atoms per impact and the substrate sputters through it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <div class="card-grid">
        <span class="card-id">H3</span>
        <p class="card-stmt">GNP nanoscale roughness geometrically shadows grazing-angle flux</p>
        <div class="card-divider">
          <span class="card-verdict card-verdict--confirmed">Confirmed</span>
          <p class="card-evidence">Reproduces the suppression of the 60–75° Mo yield peak via RustBCA + Gaussian facet-tilt convolution (σ=15°).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <div class="card-grid">
        <span class="card-id">H4</span>
        <p class="card-stmt">GNP edge-rich morphology elevates field-emission / vacuum-breakdown risk</p>
        <div class="card-divider">
          <span class="card-verdict card-verdict--warning">Design-limiting</span>
          <p class="card-evidence">Onset field drops from 7.3 → 2.3 MV/m. Fowler–Nordheim Weibull model confirms this is potentially design-limiting and partially negates the erosion benefit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <div class="callout">
      <p class="kicker">Key Insight</p>
      <h2>H2 Reversal: The Graphene Paradox</h2>
      <p>Intuition suggests an ultra-hard 2D coating should protect the substrate. Crystalline MD shows the opposite. A heavy Xe ion at CEX energies passes <em>through</em> the monolayer, depositing momentum in the Mo substrate; the low-thermal-coupling sheet cannot dissipate the cascade, so it ejects several carbon atoms per impact <em>and</em> the substrate sputters through it.</p>
      <p class="highlight">The coating adds an erosion channel instead of removing one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <p class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">Program Phases</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Content</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="mono">I</td><td>MATLAB prototype</td><td><span class="text-muted">Superseded</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">II</td><td>VIOT-2 GPU PIC-MCC prototype</td><td><span class="text-muted">Superseded — 15 defects found</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">III</td><td>VIOT-3 axisymmetric production framework</td><td class="text-navy">Complete, 70/70 tests</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">IV</td><td>VIOT-4 3D + DSMC + MD framework</td><td class="text-navy">Core complete, 2/2 tests</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">V</td><td>Consolidated manuscript</td><td class="text-navy">Complete (35 pp)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <p class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Program Scope</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <h3>In Scope</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Relative material rankings for barrel erosion and EBS lifetime</li>
          <li>Atomistic yield derivation (RustBCA + LAMMPS MD)</li>
          <li>Field-emission and thermomechanical risk screening</li>
          <li>3D framework construction and verification</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Explicitly Out of Scope</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Absolute wear rates</li>
          <li>ELT-validated lifetimes</li>
          <li>Dynamic erosion-coupled mesh evolution</li>
          <li>In-loop DSMC coupling (pending)</li>
          <li>Flight qualification of any coating</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
